# Core conventions

- Start each session by reading `docs/progress.md` and the spec or task card you were given.
- Work on ONE task card at a time. Do not touch files outside its scope.
- Minimal diffs: change only what the task requires. No drive-by refactors.
- Short comment on every function: purpose, non-obvious inputs/outputs, side effects.
- No new dependency without stating why in the PR/commit message.
- Every behavior change ships with tests; run them before declaring the task done.
- The app must start after every task. Never leave `main` broken: the E2E smoke test must pass before merge, but ask the user before running it (see `guardrails.mdc`).
- Build features as vertical slices (DB → API → UI → test) so something works end to end after each slice.
- Config comes from env (validated at startup). Never commit secrets.
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` unless justified in a comment.
- If the spec is unclear or wrong, stop and ask instead of guessing.
